# 00 — Project context: Passion Hotel PMS API

## Purpose
Orient every change in `passion-api` around what this codebase actually is, so Cursor does not
apply generic Laravel assumptions.

## When it applies
Always, for any task in the `passion-api` repository.

## Existing project convention
- Laravel 12 (slim `bootstrap/app.php` skeleton, no `Http/Kernel.php`, no `Exceptions/Handler.php`), PHP `^8.2`.
- Pure JSON API consumed by the separate Next.js app in `../passion`. Also serves DomPDF/CSV/XLSX
  downloads and Laravel Reverb broadcasts.
- **Single property.** There is no `hotel_id`, `property_id` or `tenant_id` anywhere. The only
  partition is the F&B outlet (`restaurant_masters`), enforced in POS / day closing.
- MySQL in real environments, `APP_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata` ("hotel wall time").
- Auth: Sanctum personal access tokens. Roles/permissions: Spatie, guard `web`.
- Full factual reference: `PASSION_LARAVEL_ARCHITECTURE.md` (repo root). Section numbers there
  match topics (e.g. §32 reservations, §33 availability, §34 check-in/out, §35 billing, §36 housekeeping).
- Topic rules: `.cursor/rules/grn-frozen-cost.mdc` (GRN inventory cost is read-only from frozen
  fields), `.cursor/rules/55-pos.mdc` (POS outlet access, business date, day closing).

## Required behavior
- Treat the existing implementation as the source of truth. Before changing a module, read the
  controller / Support / Service class that already owns that behavior.
- Keep diffs minimal and local to the module being changed.
- Assume the frontend in `../passion` reads the current JSON keys, status strings, permission names
  and broadcast event names. Changing any of them is a cross-repo change; call it out.
- When unsure whether behavior is intentional, list it as a question instead of "fixing" it.
- After a behavior change, create or update the functional doc for that feature
  (see `65-functional-docs.mdc`).

## Things Cursor must NOT do
- Do not add tenant/hotel/property scoping, columns or global scopes.
- Do not refactor or reorganize files you were not asked to touch (e.g. splitting
  `PosController`, `BookingController` or `HousekeepingController`).
- Do not rename routes, JSON keys, permission names, status values or event names.
- Do not "clean up" root-level artifacts (`debug_*.php`, `fix_plan.md`, `passion_db`, `scripts/*`)
  or `app/Models/Role.php` / `Permission.php` without being asked.

## Important examples from the existing codebase
- Largest logic owners: `app/Http/Controllers/PosController.php`, `BookingController.php`,
  `HousekeepingController.php`.
- Shared reservation rules: `app/Support/BookingRoomAvailability.php`,
  `app/Support/BookingPaymentLedger.php`, `app/Support/BookingCancellationPolicy.php`.
- Accounting atomicity: `app/Services/Accounting/LedgerBackedTransaction.php`,
  `app/Services/Accounting/JournalPostingService.php`.
